**Step 1: Identify the pretreatments.**
Looking at Section 2.1 "Pretreatment of pine needle litter forest biomass":
- "A three step methodology involving sequential physicochemical pretreatment viz. milling, steam explosion and acid-base-acid pretreatment was employed."
- "The physical methods included grinding (milling) the dried pine needles in an electric blender."
- "Another method employed was steam explosion of pine needles, which involved autoclaving of pine needles in flask plugged with non-absorbent cotton at 121 °C for 30 min."
- "The chemical method employed the use of repeated exposure of LCB to acid (HCl) and alkali (NaOH) (acid–base–acid treatment) with 30 min cycle, until the wash out liquid was clear. This was followed with repeated washings with water until neutral pH of the wash out liquid was obtained."

